From ada1ddf2b6fc46c382f544510d9f7212d391ed15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Otavio Salvador <otavio@ossystems.com.br>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:00:08 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] feat: approve a project's .envrc once and load it
 automatically

Loading only .envrc files allowed from a shell left every new worktree blocked until a setup
script ran direnv allow, which competes with the project's own setup script. T3 Code now asks
once per project and per .envrc content, records the approval, and writes direnv's allow record
for the exact content reviewed in each checkout it loads. A change asks again with a diff unless
the project trusts changes, a direnv deny is never overridden, and an .envrc too large to show
cannot be approved in the app.

Agent sessions pick up an approved change by restarting, but only while the whole session is
idle, so turns and background work in threads sharing the process are never cut off.
